    in_dialogue_with: "This concept enters into an active, fruitful dialogue with Western logocentrism and linguistic idealism. While Western logocentrism and linguistic idealism often seeks to analyze truth through a specific, structured lens, Sabda-Brahman expands this view by highlighting the relational, intuitive, or contextual dimensions of understanding. This comparison reveals that different traditions often converge on the same fundamental problems of existence, using different vocabularies to express a shared human search for meaning.",
