    in_dialogue_with: "This concept enters into an active, fruitful dialogue with evolutionary biology and self-actualization psychology. While evolutionary biology and self-actualization psychology often seeks to analyze truth through a specific, structured lens, Will to Power expands this view by highlighting the relational, intuitive, or contextual dimensions of understanding. This comparison reveals that different traditions often converge on the same fundamental problems of existence, using different vocabularies to express a shared human search for meaning.",
    critique: "The primary criticism leveled against Will to Power within the historical debates of the tradition is that it can be misused to justify authoritarianism and social Darwinism. Opponents argue that by emphasizing this perspective, the philosophy struggles to justify a stable, objective foundation for empirical science and social laws. To address this critique, subsequent thinkers in the Existentialism school had to develop complex theories of dual-level truth, showing how the ultimate and relative dimensions of reality can be harmonized without contradiction.",
