    in_dialogue_with: "This concept enters into an active, fruitful dialogue with cultural criticism and sociology. While cultural criticism and sociology often seeks to analyze truth through a specific, structured lens, Postmodern Condition expands this view by highlighting the relational, intuitive, or contextual dimensions of understanding. This comparison reveals that different traditions often converge on the same fundamental problems of existence, using different vocabularies to express a shared human search for meaning.",
    critique: "The primary criticism leveled against Postmodern Condition within the historical debates of the tradition is that it leaves us without a unified framework to address global crises. Opponents argue that by emphasizing this perspective, the philosophy struggles to justify a stable, objective foundation for empirical science and social laws. To address this critique, subsequent thinkers in the Postmodernism school had to develop complex theories of dual-level truth, showing how the ultimate and relative dimensions of reality can be harmonized without contradiction.",
