    in_dialogue_with: "This concept enters into an active, fruitful dialogue with intuitive insight and breakthrough thinking. While intuitive insight and breakthrough thinking often seeks to analyze truth through a specific, structured lens, Sudden Awakening expands this view by highlighting the relational, intuitive, or contextual dimensions of understanding. This comparison reveals that different traditions often converge on the same fundamental problems of existence, using different vocabularies to express a shared human search for meaning.",
    critique: "The primary criticism leveled against Sudden Awakening within the historical debates of the tradition is that it can make patient practice and study look redundant. Opponents argue that by emphasizing this perspective, the philosophy struggles to justify a stable, objective foundation for empirical science and social laws. To address this critique, subsequent thinkers in the Zen Buddhism school had to develop complex theories of dual-level truth, showing how the ultimate and relative dimensions of reality can be harmonized without contradiction.",
