    in_dialogue_with: "This concept enters into an active, fruitful dialogue with deep ecology and environmental ethics. While deep ecology and environmental ethics often seeks to analyze truth through a specific, structured lens, Safuu expands this view by highlighting the relational, intuitive, or contextual dimensions of understanding. This comparison reveals that different traditions often converge on the same fundamental problems of existence, using different vocabularies to express a shared human search for meaning.",
    critique: "The primary criticism leveled against Safuu within the historical debates of the tradition is that it can lead to conservative resistance against scientific or social change. Opponents argue that by emphasizing this perspective, the philosophy struggles to justify a stable, objective foundation for empirical science and social laws. To address this critique, subsequent thinkers in the Oromo Philosophy school had to develop complex theories of dual-level truth, showing how the ultimate and relative dimensions of reality can be harmonized without contradiction.",
